@crew ueda-vera
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello. Ueda, Watch. You'll find me early to dinner and early to bed.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. I'm writing home tonight. Can I say I met you?
- Hi there, {me}. Quiet day. I like quiet days.
? tier>=friend
- Oh, hello, {me}. I put you in my letter home. Mum says hello back.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- A letter came from Valo. On paper. It took six weeks. Worth it.
? mood:low
- Long shift. I'll write a long letter. It helps, somehow.
== near
? habit:musician
- Music room's free. I'll play one piece, then bed. Short concerts are my speciality.   #funny
? act:leisure
- My telescope's tiny next to the big one. It still finds the moon.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I write home to Valo every rest day, on paper. Tariq and I share the post bag.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Writing letters. Proper paper, slow words. When it arrives, the news is old and lovely.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Good evening, {me}. Early dinner, early bed. I'm halfway there.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh, {me}. I've missed seeing you about. I hope all's well.

== near
? habit:runner
- I run now. Slowly. I think in letters while I run. Dear Mum, my legs hurt.   #funny
? place:mess
- I like the end table. People drift over. Nobody eats alone there.

== invite
- Observatory night? Bring a coat. My telescope's small, but it's very keen.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Friday jam? I'll play one piece before bed. A short concert. Come early.   #funny

== accept
- Yes. Thank you. I'll be there.
- Oh, yes. I'll put it in my letter. "Went out. Had a nice time."   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. Early bed. I'm sorry. Another evening?
? weekday:wed|thu
- Rest day. I'm writing home to Valo. It's a long letter this week. Friday?

== missed
- You didn't come. That's all right. I wrote a little more of my letter.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday, {me}. It's going in my letter. Valo will know in six weeks.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Mum's card came. She sent it six weeks early, so it would be on time.   #warm

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's in. Stay near people tonight. That's my advice. It's good advice.

== hint
- {me}. Have you a minute later? There's something I'd like to talk through.

== about
? aff:varga-tariq:friend
- Tariq and I share the post bag to Valo. His letters are thicker. Mine are neater.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: top-up (bye, greet by time, life at friend tier)
== bye
- Goodnight, {me}. Well. Good evening. I'll be asleep soon.   #funny
- Take care. I'll mention you in my letter.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}. I've a letter half written. You're in paragraph two.
== life
? tier>=friend
- A letter's slow, so you choose the words twice. I like choosing the words twice.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Letter home. Paragraph two.
- Six weeks to Valo, by post.
- One piece, then bed. A short concert.   #funny
? time:evening
- Early dinner, early bed.
? act:off
- Rest day. Paper and ink.
?

== rumour
- Slowly, then. Here's the news.
- It'll be in my letter. You hear it first.

// Writer 4, batch 11: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Letters first. Then the telescope. Then the rest.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm leaving soon. I'll write. On paper, slowly. As I always do.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- You always waited for me to finish a sentence. That's a kind thing. Thank you for it.   #warm

== letter
- New ship. The post bag is slower here. I'm learning to like it. The telescope came safe.
? tier>=friend
- A paper letter, for once, by Mail. The Wren's out there somewhere, in my little telescope. Hello.
